bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_rtl_run_pen_phase_residual_2026-11-28, 0, "Chrome 159 at 1x, 8 px Liberation Sans, color #111827, a 96 px wide div with direction:rtl holding ABC: Chrome's glyphs sit a fraction of a px to the left of the engine's (ink grid, Chrome A at x 80..85, B 86..90, C 92..96; engine A from 81). Against a Chrome capture of the ltr and rtl lines (px with a channel delta over 8) the ltr line went 48 -> 29 and the rtl line 88 -> 84 with the Latin autohinter port; the 84 px left on the rtl line are this pen phase, not the outline (the same glyphs on the ltr line match closely)."
    web_render_rtl_run_pen_phase_residual_2026-11-28, 1, "Pin: browser_renderer_spec 'renders direction rtl Latin text in logical glyph order, end-anchored' counts non-white px. Engine ltr 84 (Chrome 86), rtl 86 (Chrome 87); the rtl pin moved 87 -> 86 with the port by owner decision 2026-11-28 (one faint fringe px). The pin should return to Chrome's 87 / 86 pair when the end-anchored run takes Chrome's pen."

